<title>SRI LANKA: Merchant Bank falls on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Merchant Bank falls on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profit-taking by small investors pushed down Merchant Bank of Sri Lanka Ltd by 5.2 percent, or 1.25 rupees, to 22.75 rupees on turnover of 1,000 shares, brokers said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Because the scrip is cheap and liquid, it is favoured by retailers,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Many small investors who got in when the share was around 20 rupees about 10 days ago are taking profit, he said.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
